SUMMARY:Natural and Human History of White Pines
DESCRIPTION:Join TLC to explore the unique history and ecosystem of White Pines Nature Preserve!\nThis 3.5 mile hike will focus on the identification and natural history of pine species found\, as well as the human history of this preserve. We'll also take the time to enjoy the beautiful scenery at the confluence of the Deep and Rocky Rivers. This hike includes variable terrain and an elevation gain of about 300 feet. This is a free event\, but preregistration is required.\n\n 
URL:https://triangleland.org/event/natural-and-human-history-of-white-pines-2
LOCATION:White Pines Nature Preserve\, 548 S Rocky River Rd\, Sanford\, NC\, 27330\, United States
ORGANIZER;CN="Amaya Horner":MAILTO:ahorner@triangleland.org
END:VEVENT
