SUMMARY:Fall Foliage Hike
DESCRIPTION:Enjoy a morning of "Leaf Peeping" at Old Creedmoor Nature Preserve!\nWe'll explore the rolling and winding multi-use trails with the reds\, oranges\, and yellows of fall as our backdrop. Old Creedmoor Nature Preserve's hardwood forest will make this a spectacular hike to see the foliage!\n\nThis 3.1 mile hike includes some narrow\, rocky\, and rooted sections of trail and steep inclines. Hikers should expect to step off the trail to share space with mountain bikers. This is a free event but preregistration is required.\n\n\n\n\n\nInclement Weather Policy: In the event of inclement weather\, you will be contacted by email for a call on cancellation or postponement.
URL:https://triangleland.org/event/fall-foliage-hike
LOCATION:Old Creedmoor Nature Preserve\, 13509 Old Creedmoor Rd\, Wake Forest\, NC\, 27587\, United States
ORGANIZER;CN="Amaya Horner":MAILTO:ahorner@triangleland.org
END:VEVENT
